- {"id": "F1", "severity": "high", "path": "scripts/parity_check.py:52", "evidence": "Live and bulk queries use timestamp-derived filename substrings without constraining them to the test folder or establishing the pre-change count. An unrelated indexed file with the same token can satisfy a create check, and a delete check can pass at zero when the corresponding create was never indexed. A failed earlier check does not prevent later checks from being reported as successful.", "fix": "Use a unique per-run token and constrain every live query to the test directory. Verify the expected pre-change count and require the intended transition before reporting each check as passed."}
- {"id": "F2", "severity": "high", "path": "scripts/parity_check.py:35", "evidence": "The timer starts inside wait_for, after the filesystem operation. Bulk creation may take longer than five seconds before timing begins. The new-name check starts only after the old-name check has completed, so a rename taking more than five seconds overall can still pass the new-name check.", "fix": "Record a monotonic timestamp immediately before each filesystem operation and measure every resulting assertion against that same timestamp, including bulk creation and both sides of a rename."}
- {"id": "F3", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/parity_check.py:68", "evidence": "The parent-folder rename check creates tok_c only after renaming the folder. It can pass when indexing a newly created child works even if the index never updates the paths of files that existed before the parent rename.", "fix": "Create and verify a child before renaming its parent, then check that its old path disappears and its new path appears within the limit."}
- {"id": "F4", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/parity_check.py:102", "evidence": "Cleanup uses shutil.rmtree(ROOT, ignore_errors=True), so a permission or filesystem error can leave the test tree behind while the script exits successfully. The cleanup is also registered only after os.makedirs(ROOT) returns, leaving a small interruption window after creation.", "fix": "Register cleanup around root creation, report cleanup errors as failures, and verify that the owned directory was removed before returning success."}
- {"id": "F5", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/install.sh:56", "evidence": "grep -qF checks for a substring in the flattened list of paths, so an existing item such as ~/Applications/MacEverything.app.backup suppresses creation of the actual app login item. If the System Events listing fails, the same condition treats the list as empty and attempts to add an item even when one may already exist.", "fix": "Compare each login item's path for exact equality in System Events, distinguish a listing error from an absent item, and do not add an item when presence cannot be determined."}
- {"id": "F6", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/install.sh:57", "evidence": "APP_PATH is interpolated directly into an AppleScript string literal. A home path containing a double quote or backslash changes the AppleScript source, causing the add operation to fail or be interpreted incorrectly.", "fix": "Pass the path as an osascript argument and read it from argv, rather than interpolating it into AppleScript source."}
