- {"id": "F1", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/parity_check.py:80", "evidence": "The move check verifies only that the file appears under live/sub. If the index adds the destination but retains the old live/ entry, this check passes even though the move was not fully reflected.", "fix": "Check both the disappearance of the old path and the appearance of the new path. Use a query that distinguishes a direct child of live from a descendant under live/sub."}
- {"id": "F2", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/parity_check.py:108", "evidence": "The speed check passes based on the median of five runs. For example, three 50 ms searches and two 500 ms searches pass, although the stated bar requires every search to answer under 100 ms.", "fix": "Fail when any measured search reaches or exceeds 100 ms; the median can still be reported as additional context."}
- {"id": "F3", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/parity_check.py:32", "evidence": "subprocess.run has no timeout, and the ev client waits for the daemon response without setting a read timeout in Sources/EverythingCore/IPC.swift. If the daemon accepts a request but stops responding, WAIT_CAP cannot be reached, the checker never exits, and its cleanup does not run.", "fix": "Give each ev invocation a bounded timeout, turn a timeout into a reported failure, and allow control to reach the cleanup block."}
- {"id": "F4", "severity": "low", "path": "scripts/parity_check.py:28", "evidence": "The path filter is a substring, so it also matches another indexed directory named MacEverything-paritytest outside the home folder. The PID-and-second token reduces collisions but does not guarantee uniqueness; an unrelated matching file can satisfy a target count.", "fix": "Use a high-entropy run token and scope queries to the full test-root path with appropriate query quoting. Ensure generated names cannot collide with unrelated indexed files."}
